  "name": "Convoke Rage",
  "type": "spell",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Requirements</strong> Your Domain Convocation is active and you and your convocator are within line of effect of each other.</p><hr></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">You channel the rage of your domain into a singular attack delivered by your convocator. You form magic from your sacred pact that manifests in your convocator, who can either unleash a ranged spell attack at a creature within 60 feet of both of you, using the greater of you or your convocator’s spell attack modifier, or Stride and make a melee Strike at a creature they can reach with their movement.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Regardless of your choice, the magic erupts on a successful hit, dealing 3d6 damage of the same type as your Primary Domain’s damage type, doubled on a critical hit. If you use a ranged spell attack, you also add half the number of damage die’s worth of d6 rounded down as persistent damage.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Heightened (+1) </strong>Increase the magic’s damage by 1d6.</p>"
    },
